- Yeah.

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:17.280
Oh my gosh. I mean there's other ones.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.300
- Does it get worse?

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.590
- It gets different.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.030
It's like, but it's awesome.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.740
I love, my daughter was
curious like that too

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.560
and I mean she's totally
gonna give me gray hair

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.755
but she's also-
- I definitely have it.

00:01:27.755 --> 00:01:28.614
- like super bold.
- Yeah.

00:01:28.614 --> 00:01:29.996
- And I love that from a young age.

00:01:29.996 --> 00:01:31.890
Like even when she was
like one I could tell,

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.820
I was like, she's gonna have a
very good sense of who she is

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.080
and like very bold and brave.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:37.967
- [Priyanka] What's what I feel.

00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:38.800
- You'll love that.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:39.633
- I feel like she's brave.

00:01:39.633 --> 00:01:40.620
She knows exactly what she wants.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.720
- Yeah. But it's also
gonna give you gray hair.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.980
- Yeah.
- Me too.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.720
- I think it's starting.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.030
- Nick said that he sings to her, right?

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.200
- Yes.
- I think that's adorable.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.120
Like even whenever like
she was in the womb, right?

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.230
- Yes.
- That's adorable.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.063
What kind of music?

00:01:53.063 --> 00:01:53.896
What tunes?

00:01:53.896 --> 00:01:57.000
- When we were in, I mean
for those who don't know,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.830
we had a really rough journey with Malti

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:02.654
and she was in the NICU
for about 110 days.

00:02:02.654 --> 00:02:03.487
- I didn't know that.

00:02:03.487 --> 00:02:06.270
- And pretty much the
whole third trimester.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.370
And Nick used to go in with his guitar

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.470
and I mean, sing to her.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.434
I played my audiobook, you know?

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.680
(laughing)

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.282
Or movies. I couldn't compete.

00:02:15.282 --> 00:02:16.650
- [Kelly] I was like, you could sing.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.910
- Not like that.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.440
- Yes you can.
- Oh.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.820
- It's mama's voice. Yeah.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.050
- Yeah. But I mean I did,

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.640
she's the only fan of my voice.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:24.900
She like loves when I sing.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:25.920
The only person in the world

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.030
And I love it.
- You're such a liar.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.260
You are such a liar.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.700
So wait, you and Nick have a ritual

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:30.533
that I didn't know about.

00:02:30.533 --> 00:02:31.560
So it's called Show and Tell.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.540
This is pretty cute. Explain it.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.930
- It kind of isn't a ritual,

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.810
it just happened because of necessity.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.240
We both didn't know very much
about each other's careers.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.860
I mean I know of the Jonas Brothers

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.780
but you know, it's a different generation.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.630
I was like, I didn't really
grow up with the music.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:46.463
- Yeah.

00:02:46.463 --> 00:02:47.730
- I didn't know the
history even though him

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.470
and I both have 22 year careers

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.090
'cause he started his at seven.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.200
- Yeah.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.110
- But so we started showing
each other, each other's work.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.017
Like we would sit and be like,

00:02:56.017 --> 00:02:59.640
"Oh you know this was the
most traumatic day on set

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:00.960
for me when my first movie."

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.240
And he was like, "Oh, this
was my most traumatic show."

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.390
And we'd kind of show
each other our careers

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:07.440
or highlights from our careers

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.450
and talk about what we were
really feeling that time.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.940
And it's just become this
thing that we do whenever.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:12.773
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:03:12.773 --> 00:03:14.040
- We're by ourselves at home.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.110
We just go down the rabbit hole.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.330
- 'Cause y'all met and y'all
got together pretty quickly,

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.163
right?
- Yeah.

00:03:19.163 --> 00:03:20.100
- So it's kind of cool you get

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.450
to know each other like still.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.000
- Yeah. I mean we knew each
other for about two years.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:24.833
- Yeah.

00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:27.240
- But we didn't like really date.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.430
We were both in other things.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.320
- Like other jobs and stuff.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.305
- No, other relationships.

00:03:32.305 --> 00:03:33.392
- Oh, other relationships. Oh yeah.

00:03:33.392 --> 00:03:34.225
(laughing)

00:03:34.225 --> 00:03:36.690
Totally. Thought you mean jobs.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.820
- I was trying to be subtle.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.470
- We both weren't sure.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.610
I think that's awesome though.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.260
Like to show like, I don't know,

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.880
I just think it's a very cute way

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.770
to like get to know your significant other

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.390
that you think you know everything about.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.853
But they weren't there
for that whole time.

00:03:49.853 --> 00:03:50.686
- They weren't, right?

00:03:50.686 --> 00:03:52.770
And I think it's such a fun thing to,

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.780
especially both of us have
had such public careers.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:57.592
We've both grown up in our own way

00:03:57.592 --> 00:03:58.425
in front of other people.
- I love that you both

00:03:58.425 --> 00:03:59.400
didn't know each other's careers either.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.233
- I know. It's so crazy.

00:04:00.233 --> 00:04:01.066
- That's kind of cool.

00:04:01.066 --> 00:04:01.899
- I think so too.

00:04:01.899 --> 00:04:02.790
- Yeah.
- It's really fun.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:03.810
Like, you know-

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:04.643
- [Kelly] You're there for
the right reason, both of you.

00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:06.420
- And we show each other
our embarrassing moments

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.590
'cause you know, that's your person

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.575
and you're safe with them.

00:04:09.575 --> 00:04:10.408
- And it's funny.

00:04:10.408 --> 00:04:11.241
- And I can show him
like my bad performances

00:04:11.241 --> 00:04:12.870
and be able to laugh at it.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.010
- Oh, me too. I have plenty.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:15.990
Well you turned 40 this past year?

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.160
I always forget we're the same age.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.350
So do you feel different?
(audience cheering)

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.360
I feel like once I hit 40,

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.190
I feel like I like life a lot better.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.720
The more I mature, I like life.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.250
But like, I think it's just better.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.420
It's easier, you're wiser,

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.760
but like, also like things hurt.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:30.593
- Yes.

00:04:30.593 --> 00:04:32.250
- That didn't hurt or you
can't bounce back as quickly.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.750
- Oh, definitely not.
- Yeah.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.493
- The one thing that happened after 40 was

00:04:37.493 --> 00:04:39.000
I like to incubate a lot more.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.890
I like spending time
with myself, my family.

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:44.190
My priorities have suddenly
become really clear.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.873
I don't sweat the little stuff.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.930
But also your metabolism takes a big hit.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:53.160
You're like, oh, I see that
sandwich for the next week.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.088
- Yeah.

00:04:54.088 --> 00:04:54.990
- You know, or that pizza.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.910
And I love food. I live for food.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:57.743
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:04:57.743 --> 00:04:59.765
- I know, but my job is not-

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.440
Like, doesn't like the fact

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.550
that I love food as much as I do.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:06.510
So that changes, your relationship
with your body changes.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.470
I used to work a lot.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.000
I still do, I work a lot.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.013
I love my job. I feel very good.

00:05:10.013 --> 00:05:11.370
- Me too. I like working.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.203
- I love working.
- Me too.

00:05:12.203 --> 00:05:13.036
- I love my job.

00:05:13.036 --> 00:05:14.730
But you know, you get tired.
- Yeah.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.807
- You wanna go home
and like nap. You know?

00:05:15.807 --> 00:05:17.730
- I'm really looking forward to napping.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:18.690
After the show, yeah.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:19.620
- A nap would be nice.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.000
- And a nap, I mean by like sleep,

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.727
like solid eight hours.
- That's so so old, Kelly.

00:05:22.727 --> 00:05:25.590
- Yeah. I don't know
why I said nap, really.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.423
I mean usually I think

00:05:26.423 --> 00:05:28.110
because I don't get a full
night's rest and I need it.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.360
But like, no, I just
mean a full night's rest.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.650
I'm very excited about that tonight.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:32.560
- Yeah. To be able to leave eight hours.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:33.600
- Eight hours.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.120
Oh, you get it. Well,
you have a one year old.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:36.953
You might not get that.

00:05:36.953 --> 00:05:38.670
- [Priyanka] It's hard. It's hard.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.487
- we're back with Priyanka
Chopra Jonas, y'all. Give it up.

00:05:41.487 --> 00:05:42.426
(audience cheering)

00:05:42.426 --> 00:05:43.390
Your new movie is called "Love Again".

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.690
So why did you wanna be a part of it?

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.570
- It's just, first of all, it's
Celine Dion's acting debut.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.403
- [Kelly] I know.

00:05:49.403 --> 00:05:50.236
That's incredible.
- How crazy.

00:05:50.236 --> 00:05:51.445
For the rest of time,

00:05:51.445 --> 00:05:52.560
I'll be in her first movie
- I never knew she'd do it.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:53.393
Yeah, that's incredible.

00:05:53.393 --> 00:05:55.440
- I just can't believe she hasn't done it.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.547
- I guess I can't either.
- You know?

00:05:56.547 --> 00:05:57.570
You would think that Celine--

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:58.590
She's so funny.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:05:59.423
- Very passionate.

00:05:59.423 --> 00:06:00.810
- She's super passionate.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:03.630
She came in like such a
professional on this movie.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.210
She helps me and Sam's
character find love.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.890
And we have original music from Celine,

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:10.410
which we haven't had
for a really long time.

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:13.620
And she's grappling with some health stuff

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:14.940
so I'm just really excited

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.560
to be able to, you know, see her

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.870
and have her fans see
her again in the movie.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:19.770
So that was a big reason.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.350
But also this movie's a
remake of a German film

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.180
and it's just so sweet.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.680
I love a great romcom.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:26.513
- Me too.

00:06:26.513 --> 00:06:28.054
- I love like, you know
what makes your heart smile.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:28.887
- They don't make enough of them.

00:06:28.887 --> 00:06:29.910
- Yeah. We don't.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.380
And I love that moment of being able

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:33.510
to go into the theater,
getting like a bag of popcorn

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:34.560
and sitting and watching a movie

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.590
that makes you feel hopeful and happy.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:38.613
And you find love again.

00:06:38.613 --> 00:06:40.175
- It's the opposite of watching the news.

00:06:40.175 --> 00:06:41.070
- [Priyanka] Who doesn't
wanna find love again?

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.855
- Yes. Some of us don't, but-

00:06:42.855 --> 00:06:43.784
(laughing)

00:06:43.784 --> 00:06:44.880
- Facts.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:45.713
- But Nick is also in the movie.

00:06:45.713 --> 00:06:46.546
- In different ways.

00:06:46.546 --> 00:06:47.379
- Yeah. Nick is also in the movie.

00:06:47.379 --> 00:06:48.212
I didn't know that.

00:06:48.212 --> 00:06:49.045
So was he just there with you?

00:06:49.045 --> 00:06:50.865
And then y'all are just
like, "Hey, come do this".

00:06:50.865 --> 00:06:51.698
- Kind of.

00:06:51.698 --> 00:06:53.284
- Okay. I love this.

00:06:53.284 --> 00:06:54.117
- Kind of.

00:06:54.117 --> 00:06:54.950
I was moving to London.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.300
This was 2020 and it was like during,

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.850
like in the middle of Covid.
- Covid, yeah.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.640
- And Nick was like, "No, I'm
gonna come to London with you,

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.410
make sure you're settled
and then come back."

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.930
So he was kind of there
with me to support.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.787
And I was filming and
the producers were like,

00:07:09.787 --> 00:07:11.550
"Well Nick's here, do you mind?

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:12.750
Can we? Do you think we could?"

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:14.160
Ah, ah.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.570
And I was actually really grateful

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.490
that they wanted to ask him.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:20.640
Because the scene as it
was written is a bad date.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.760
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.359
(Kelly laughing)

00:07:23.359 --> 00:07:27.570
- [Priyanka] And it's slow
slobbery kissing with an actor.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:29.487
- [Kelly] Look at Nick's face. (chuckling)

00:07:29.487 --> 00:07:30.900
- And it was written like that

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.520
and I had to do it with a stranger

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.850
like a random person
slobbering slowly on my face.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.010
- No. I've had to do
that in a music video.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:40.050
And I have a thing with
saliva. It was a hard day.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:40.883
- [Priyanka] I don't do that.

00:07:40.883 --> 00:07:42.150
- That'd be my traumatic thing.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:43.650
I'd show my significant other.

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:45.596
- I can't do that.

00:07:45.596 --> 00:07:47.490
So I was so grateful that Nick,

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.350
first of all, was approached.
- He's licking your face.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.461
- And second of all, that it
was my husband that did it.

00:07:51.461 --> 00:07:53.333
So I was like, phew. Dodged that bullet.

00:07:53.333 --> 00:07:54.960
- Which kinda makes it like
so funny for everybody.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.100
That little nugget in the movie

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.860
of like, you're like not
interested in your husband.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:07:59.693
- It's so funny.

00:07:59.693 --> 00:08:00.570
- It's funny.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:01.890
So speaking of movies though,

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.950
you and I are now the only
people with our own flavors

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.522
of Rob's Backstage Popcorn.

00:08:07.522 --> 00:08:08.355
(audience cheering)

00:08:08.355 --> 00:08:10.650
Rob's backstage. This
is mine, this is yours.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:11.610
I wanna try yours.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.443
- You haven't tried it?

00:08:12.443 --> 00:08:13.841
- No, I haven't been able to try it.

00:08:13.841 --> 00:08:14.674
- Oh.

00:08:14.674 --> 00:08:15.661
- I asked Nick he was like,

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:16.901
"We'll get you some".
- I think it's very important

00:08:16.901 --> 00:08:18.350
for the Rob's, all of the flavors.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.422
- Oh you have to shame 'em?
- You have to.

00:08:20.422 --> 00:08:21.255
- Get all the stuff around.

00:08:21.255 --> 00:08:22.088
- Yeah, get all the juices.

00:08:22.088 --> 00:08:23.011
- I'll have of mine too.

00:08:23.011 --> 00:08:24.360
We can share mine.
- Yeah, yours too.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.455
- Wow. That was really loud.

00:08:25.455 --> 00:08:26.288
Did you hear that?
- Yours is amazing.

00:08:26.288 --> 00:08:28.470
- It was like (imitates bag popping)

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.670
I'm used to being on TV, guys,

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:31.080
I promise.
- Hey.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.070
Look at that barbecue, guys.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.660
- It's called Mumbai Night?

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:34.493
Mumbai Nights.

00:08:34.493 --> 00:08:35.520
- It's called Mumbai Nights.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:36.813
Because, so yummy.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:41.220
Because it reminds me of the Mumbai heat.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.920
Mumbai is very humid and
this has like a kick to it.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:44.760
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.470
- Indian Spice blend.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:49.680
I use some of my favorite
spices like turmeric and-

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:50.970
- Girl, this is good

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:51.803
- Right?

00:08:51.803 --> 00:08:52.710
- I love turmeric

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.530
- And like cumin and garlic and onion.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:56.363
- [Kelly] I'm just gonna keep eating.

00:08:56.363 --> 00:08:57.196
- Keep eating. It's great.

00:08:57.196 --> 00:08:58.100
- You keep talking.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:08:59.933
Oh, they're really good.

00:08:59.933 --> 00:09:01.680
You have a new series too,
it's called "Citadel".

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:02.513
- Yes, I do.

00:09:02.513 --> 00:09:03.346
- I love this. I'm excited about this.

00:09:03.346 --> 00:09:04.179
What is it about?

00:09:04.179 --> 00:09:06.930
- It's on Amazon Prime
and it is a spy show.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:07.830
It's out there now.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.390
You guys should check it out.
- I love spies shows.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:10.680
- It's a really great spy show.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:13.833
It's got Richard Madden,
Stanley Tucci, me.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:15.623
- Great cast.

00:09:15.623 --> 00:09:17.400
- An amazing cast of people.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:22.080
But it's six episodes and
it's a really sick show.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.450
There's never been anything at the scale

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.880
of like action stunts

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.470
and of the production value of the show.

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:29.303
But at the same time,

00:09:29.303 --> 00:09:31.260
it has real heart with characters.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:34.950
Like my character and
Richard's character have drama.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.965
We have history plus we
have to save the world

00:09:37.965 --> 00:09:39.390
and then have to do it together.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.530
- I'm into all that.

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:42.060
- It's so good because of all of that.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.380
- Is the action hard for you?
(audience clapping)

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.410
Like the scenes, like the action scenes?

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.340
I feel like you're always in things

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:49.080
when you're doing stuff
like that, so I like that.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.900
- I have done a lot of
my stunts my whole life.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.510
But I've also learned to do that

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.820
because I mean, I started with,

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.470
you know, smaller Bollywood movies

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:00.750
and we never had a stunt
double that was awesome.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.040
Oh gosh.
- What?

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.600
- They're gonna kill me for that clip.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:05.040
- Oh. I'm like, wait, which--

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:05.873
Oh, okay.

00:10:05.873 --> 00:10:08.040
- [Priyanka] That's me
pole vaulting over a horse.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.540
- [Kelly] Wait, so I heard about this-

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.184
- Which didn't make the movie.
- And it didn't even make it!

00:10:11.184 --> 00:10:12.353
It didn't even make it.

00:10:12.353 --> 00:10:14.670
And you pole vaulted over a horse.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.410
- [Priyanka] Yeah, a stallion.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.286
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:17.286 --> 00:10:18.119
- [Kelly] That's a big horse.

00:10:18.119 --> 00:10:18.952
- [Priyanka] I mean, I was rigged,

00:10:18.952 --> 00:10:20.940
but it is still pole
vaulting over a horse.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:21.870
- Still looks so cool.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:22.703
- It looked amazing.

00:10:22.703 --> 00:10:25.530
- I would've fought like
hell to be in the show.

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:26.970
- It lives on my phone.

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:29.130
I watch it every couple of days.

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:29.963
- Just to remind myself I did this.

00:10:29.963 --> 00:10:31.830
- Reminds myself that I'm capable of that.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:35.820
But I love stunts and
I trust my body a lot.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.770
I've had a lot of experience doing it.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.510
But, you know, working
with the Russo brothers,

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:41.160
they have such an amazing stunt team.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.330
Like look at all the stuff they've done

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:44.130
with the Marvel stuff.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:47.640
And you know, their stunt
team taught us a lot.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.710
We trained, it was a year and a half

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.620
of training and-
- Wow.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.600
- Being prepared and working on your body

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:56.400
and learning, like there's so much,

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:57.660
so many stunts in this

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:59.220
but it makes you feel like such a sense

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.590
of achievement when you watch
the show and you're like, wow.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.483
Like 80% of that was me.
- I look bad-ass.

00:11:03.483 --> 00:11:04.317
Yeah.

00:11:04.317 --> 00:11:05.490
- And I did a great job.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:08.853
So it was challenging but
it was gratifying too.

00:11:09.863 --> 00:11:12.420
- So something I love to
hear is on your new show,

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:14.430
you actually have equal
pay with your male co-star.

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.930
- Yes.
- Yeah. I love that.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:16.763
Did you have to--

00:11:16.763 --> 00:11:17.823
You had to fight hard for that.

00:11:17.823 --> 00:11:19.192
(audience cheering)

00:11:19.192 --> 00:11:20.460
Cause I know of many of actresses

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:22.530
that have tried to do this
and it doesn't always work.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.720
That's incredible.
- No, it doesn't usually work.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.520
And there are like weird excuses for it

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:30.510
that, you know, you're
not actually co-leads

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:34.661
or you're not as accomplished
or, but in this case-

00:11:34.661 --> 00:11:36.030
- Can't hear that enough. Yeah.

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:36.863
- Yeah, I know.

00:11:36.863 --> 00:11:38.640
You know, the male actor
has accomplished a lot more

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.800
or like, there's always
some sort of debate.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.450
But I've had a 22 year career.

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:46.530
I've worked with many, many
male co-actors around the world.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:50.040
I have done many as co-leads,
which is what the show was.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:51.930
So my contract was actually done.

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:55.980
And I remember my agents
at UTA, love you guys,

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.740
went in and said, "You know,
you are a co-lead on this show.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:01.890
You should have
most-favorite-nation with Richard."

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:03.630
And I was like, "Oh really?

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.550
I mean, I guess I should, but like".

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:06.383
- That's not gonna happen.

00:12:06.383 --> 00:12:07.440
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.720
- I'm jaded enough to be like,
well that's not gonna happen.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:11.610
I'll take whatever I'll get.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:12.780
And they were like, "No, let us go back

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:15.030
and have that conversation
with the studio."

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:17.070
They went back to Amazon studios

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:18.660
and they really didn't have any pushback.

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:20.130
They were like, "You're
right, they're co-leads.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.170
They should have most-favorite-nations."

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.947
And they came back and they were like,

00:12:23.947 --> 00:12:27.360
"Well you have the same
parity and the same pay."

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:28.193
And I was like,

00:12:28.193 --> 00:12:30.180
"Wait, that happened?"
- What?

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.410
- And they were like, "Yeah, it did."

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:33.150
So there are some people that'll do that.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.241
And now Hollywood's changing.
- Way to go, Amazon.

00:12:35.241 --> 00:12:36.491
That's amazing.

